# INKAHOME - Database Schema Reference

## Entity-Relationship Overview

```mermaid
erDiagram
    User ||--o| OwnerProfile : "has"
    User ||--o| TenantProfile : "has"
    User ||--o{ CaretakerEstate : "assigned via"
    User ||--o{ PaymentAdjustment : "makes"
    User ||--o{ AuditLog : "generates"
    User ||--o{ Complaint : "approves (ComplaintApprover)"

    OwnerProfile ||--o{ Estate : "owns"

    Estate ||--o{ Unit : "contains"
    Estate ||--o{ CaretakerEstate : "managed by"
    Estate ||--o{ Complaint : "has"

    Unit ||--o| TenantProfile : "occupied by"
    Unit ||--o{ Payment : "receives"
    Unit ||--o{ MoveOutRequest : "has"

    TenantProfile ||--o{ Payment : "makes"
    TenantProfile ||--o{ Complaint : "raises"
    TenantProfile ||--o{ MoveOutRequest : "submits"

    Payment ||--o{ PaymentAdjustment : "adjusted by"
```

---

## Tables

### `users`
The central identity table. Every person in the system is a `User`.

| Column | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `id` | UUID PK | Auto-generated |
| `email` | String | Unique |
| `password_hash` | String | bcrypt hash |
| `first_name` | String | |
| `last_name` | String | |
| `phone` | String? | Optional |
| `role` | `Role` enum | Controls access |
| `is_active` | Boolean | Soft-disable accounts |
| `refresh_token_hash` | String? | For JWT refresh |
| `created_at` / `updated_at` | DateTime | Audit timestamps |

**Role Enum:** `ADMIN` · `OWNER` · `CARETAKER` · `TENANT`

---

### `owner_profiles`
Extends `User` for property owners. One owner can own many estates.

| Column | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `id` | UUID PK | |
| `user_id` | UUID FK → `users` | Unique (1-to-1) |

---

### `estates`
A property/compound owned by an owner. Contains multiple units.

| Column | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `id` | UUID PK | |
| `name` | String | Estate name |
| `address` | String | Street address |
| `city` | String | |
| `owner_id` | UUID FK → `owner_profiles` | Cascade delete |

---

### `caretaker_estates` *(junction table)*
Many-to-many link between caretakers (`users`) and estates. A caretaker can manage more than one estate; an estate can have more than one caretaker.

| Column | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `id` | UUID PK | |
| `user_id` | UUID FK → `users` | |
| `estate_id` | UUID FK → `estates` | |
| `assigned_at` | DateTime | When assignment was made |

> **Unique constraint:** `(user_id, estate_id)` — no duplicate assignments.

---

### `units`
An individual rentable unit within an estate (e.g., Apartment 3B).

| Column | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `id` | UUID PK | |
| `unit_number` | String | e.g. `"3B"` |
| `estate_id` | UUID FK → `estates` | |
| `monthly_rent` | Decimal(12,2) | Configured rent amount |
| `status` | `UnitStatus` enum | `VACANT` / `OCCUPIED` / `MAINTENANCE` |
| `description` | String? | Optional notes |

**UnitStatus Enum:** `VACANT` · `OCCUPIED` · `MAINTENANCE`

> **Unique constraint:** `(estate_id, unit_number)` — no duplicate unit numbers per estate.

---

### `tenant_profiles`
Extends `User` for tenants. Links a tenant to their unit and lease dates.

| Column | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `id` | UUID PK | |
| `user_id` | UUID FK → `users` | Unique (1-to-1) |
| `unit_id` | UUID FK → `units`? | Nullable (tenant not yet placed) |
| `lease_start` | DateTime? | Lease start date |
| `lease_end` | DateTime? | Lease expiry date |

> When a tenant moves out, `unit_id` is set to `NULL` (SetNull), preserving payment history.

---

### `payments`
**Immutable** financial records. Once created, rows are never updated — only voided.

| Column | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `id` | UUID PK | |
| `amount` | Decimal(12,2) | Amount paid |
| `unit_id` | UUID FK → `units` | Restrict delete |
| `tenant_id` | UUID FK → `tenant_profiles` | Restrict delete |
| `payment_method` | `PaymentMethod` enum | |
| `payment_date` | DateTime | Actual date of payment |
| `period_month` | Int | Billing month (1–12) |
| `period_year` | Int | Billing year (e.g. 2025) |
| `reference` | String? | e.g. M-PESA code |
| `notes` | String? | Free-text notes |
| `is_voided` | Boolean | Soft-void flag |
| `voided_at` | DateTime? | When voided |
| `voided_reason` | String? | Why voided |
| `created_at` | DateTime | **No** `updated_at` — immutable |

**PaymentMethod Enum:** `CASH` · `MPESA` · `BANK_TRANSFER` · `CHEQUE` · `OTHER`

---

### `payment_adjustments`
Correction layer on top of an immutable payment. Stores delta amounts with a reason.

| Column | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `id` | UUID PK | |
| `payment_id` | UUID FK → `payments` | |
| `amount` | Decimal(12,2) | Positive = credit, Negative = debit |
| `reason` | String | Required explanation |
| `adjusted_by` | UUID FK → `users` | Who made the adjustment |
| `created_at` | DateTime | Immutable |

---

### `complaints`
Tracks issues raised by tenants or caretakers. Doubles as an **expense tracking** record.

| Column | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `id` | UUID PK | |
| `tenant_id` | UUID FK → `tenant_profiles`? | Nullable (caretaker-raised) |
| `estate_id` | UUID FK → `estates` | |
| `subject` | String | Short title |
| `description` | String | Full details |
| `status` | `ComplaintStatus` enum | Lifecycle status |
| `source` | `ComplaintSource` enum | `TENANT` or `CARETAKER` |
| `estimated_cost` | Decimal? | Caretaker's initial estimate |
| `final_cost` | Decimal? | Actual cost after resolution |
| `expense_status` | `ExpenseStatus` enum | Approval workflow |
| `is_deductible` | Boolean | Deducted from owner payout? |
| `approved_by` | UUID FK → `users`? | Who approved the expense |
| `approved_at` | DateTime? | |
| `is_voided` | Boolean | Soft-void flag |

**ComplaintStatus Enum:** `OPEN` · `IN_PROGRESS` · `RESOLVED` · `CLOSED`  
**ExpenseStatus Enum:** `PENDING_CARETAKER` · `PENDING_OWNER` · `APPROVED` · `REJECTED`

---

### `move_out_requests`
Formal move-out process. Keeps a history of all exit requests for a unit.

| Column | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `id` | UUID PK | |
| `tenant_id` | UUID FK → `tenant_profiles` | |
| `unit_id` | UUID FK → `units` | |
| `requested_date` | DateTime | Date tenant wants to vacate |
| `reason` | String? | Optional reason |
| `status` | `MoveOutStatus` enum | |
| `is_voided` | Boolean | Soft-void flag |

**MoveOutStatus Enum:** `PENDING` · `APPROVED` · `REJECTED` · `COMPLETED`

---

### `audit_logs`
Append-only log of every significant action in the system.

| Column | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `id` | UUID PK | |
| `actor_id` | UUID FK → `users` | Who performed the action |
| `action` | String | e.g. `"CREATE"`, `"VOID_PAYMENT"` |
| `entity` | String | Table name, e.g. `"payments"` |
| `entity_id` | String | PK of the affected row |
| `before` | JSON? | Snapshot before change |
| `after` | JSON? | Snapshot after change |
| `created_at` | DateTime | Immutable |

---

## How Meaningful Information Is Derived

### 1. Rent Collection Status (per unit / per period)
```sql
-- Has this unit paid for March 2025?
SELECT *
FROM payments
WHERE unit_id = '<unit_id>'
  AND period_year = 2025
  AND period_month = 3
  AND is_voided = false;
-- No rows = UNPAID. Rows present = check SUM(amount) vs unit.monthly_rent
```
> **Effective amount paid** = `SUM(payment.amount) + SUM(adjustment.amount)` for that period.

---

### 2. Occupancy Rate (per estate)
```sql
SELECT
  COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE status = 'OCCUPIED') AS occupied,
  COUNT(*) AS total,
  ROUND(COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE status = 'OCCUPIED') * 100.0 / COUNT(*), 1) AS occupancy_pct
FROM units
WHERE estate_id = '<estate_id>';
```

---

### 3. Lease Expiry Alerts
```sql
-- Leases expiring within 30 days
SELECT u.first_name, u.last_name, tp.lease_end, un.unit_number
FROM tenant_profiles tp
JOIN users u ON u.id = tp.user_id
JOIN units un ON un.id = tp.unit_id
WHERE tp.lease_end BETWEEN NOW() AND NOW() + INTERVAL '30 days';
```

---

### 4. Total Revenue (per estate, per month)
```sql
SELECT
  SUM(p.amount) + COALESCE(SUM(pa.amount), 0) AS net_revenue
FROM payments p
LEFT JOIN payment_adjustments pa ON pa.payment_id = p.id
JOIN units u ON u.id = p.unit_id
WHERE u.estate_id = '<estate_id>'
  AND p.period_year = 2025
  AND p.period_month = 3
  AND p.is_voided = false;
```

---

### 5. Expense Flow (Complaint → Approval → Deduction)
```
Complaint raised (OPEN)
  → Caretaker sets estimated_cost (PENDING_CARETAKER)
  → Owner reviews (PENDING_OWNER → APPROVED / REJECTED)
  → If is_deductible = true: deduct final_cost from owner payout
  → Complaint RESOLVED / CLOSED
```
Query to find approved deductible expenses:
```sql
SELECT subject, final_cost, approved_at
FROM complaints
WHERE estate_id = '<estate_id>'
  AND expense_status = 'APPROVED'
  AND is_deductible = true
  AND is_voided = false;
```

---

### 6. Net Owner Payout (Revenue minus Deductible Expenses)
```
Net Payout = Total Rent Collected − Approved Deductible Expenses
```
This is computed at the application layer by combining queries 4 and 5.

---

### 7. Full Audit Trail for a Record
```sql
-- Everything that happened to a payment
SELECT actor_id, action, before, after, created_at
FROM audit_logs
WHERE entity = 'payments'
  AND entity_id = '<payment_id>'
ORDER BY created_at ASC;
```

---

### 8. Tenant Arrears Report
```sql
-- Units that have NO payment for the current month
SELECT un.unit_number, tp.user_id AS tenant_user_id
FROM units un
JOIN tenant_profiles tp ON tp.unit_id = un.id
WHERE un.estate_id = '<estate_id>'
  AND NOT EXISTS (
    SELECT 1 FROM payments p
    WHERE p.unit_id = un.id
      AND p.period_year = EXTRACT(YEAR FROM NOW())
      AND p.period_month = EXTRACT(MONTH FROM NOW())
      AND p.is_voided = false
  );
```
